# --- Large non-runtime directories (must NOT be published to GitHub Pages) ---
# build/  = data-generator scripts + their raw source inputs, incl. the 466MB ETOPO GeoTIFF.
# archive/ = backup snapshots + the original zips (ALL.zip ~535MB). Both are kept locally as
# project/dev material but would blow GitHub's 1GB-site / 100MB-file limits and bloat the repo.
build/
archive/

# Raw/working press-kit footage (source material, not deployable assets). GitHub hard-blocks any single
# file over 100MB, and press-kit/0801.mov alone is ~200MB — never let a broad `git add` catch these.
# The actual embeddable clips are press-kit/screenshots/*.mp4 (compressed, committed, referenced by
# landing.html/geo.html) — those are NOT covered by this rule.
press-kit/*.mov
press-kit/*.mp4
press-kit/_analysis/
press-kit/_clips/
!press-kit/screenshots/*.mp4

# The app only ever loads geo.html + these 5 siblings at runtime; everything committed should be
# the deployable static site (geo.html, index.html, the 5 assets, README).

# Internal dev/engineering notes (session logs, handoff docs, research write-ups). Kept locally
# for project continuity but not part of the public product — never published to the repo/Pages.
research/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
